{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>and shall lie down, the hedgehog</b> — in the language of Ishmael, קפיד." "<b>in their capitals</b> — in the shade of their capitals, like כפתור." "<b>voice</b> — the birds in the window of the walls." "<b>and the meaning of חורב בסף</b> — like \"and I will call חורב upon the earth and upon the mountains.\" The כפתור is the strongest and hardest part of the door, and if the door rots or breaks by force, the כפתור still remains, for it is the hard one. And the כפתור is known in the land of Ishmael, for it is not found among us." "<b>for the cedar has peeled</b> — this is the decking, for the חורב exposed the decking, like \"and a peeled wall for a shield.\""], :book :zephaniah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {3 "The verse citation alluded to is Amos 4:7; resolved by the quoted phrase matching that verse."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zephaniah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zfanya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:23.805734481Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}